lesson: 159
title: The bar model: the whole from the part that is left, and from a difference
level: primary-3
stars: 1
explain: Draw the whole as a bar cut into equal units. If 2/5 is spent, 2 units are gone and 3 units are left.
explain: If the 3 units left are 36 dollars, one unit is 36 ÷ 3 = 12, and the whole is 5 × 12 = 60 dollars.
explain: Comparing works the same way: if Ann has 2/5 as many as Ben, Ann has 2 units, Ben has 5, and the difference is 3 units.
vars: a=name b=name t=thing u=2..30 p=3..9 m=1..8
let: R = (p - m) * u
need: m < p
need: (m % 2 != 0 || p % 2 != 0) && (m % 3 != 0 || p % 3 != 0)
answer: p * u
exercise: {a} spent {m}/{p} of {a.his} money on a book and had {R} dollars left. How many dollars did {a.he} have at first?
exercise: {m}/{p} of the children in a class are boys. There are {R} girls. How many children are in the class?
exercise: {a} has {m}/{p} as many {t} as {b}. {b} has {R} more {t} than {a}. How many {t} does {b} have?
exercise: A farmer sold {m}/{p} of his eggs and has {R} eggs left. How many eggs did he have at first?
exercise: A short ribbon is {m}/{p} as long as a long ribbon, and it is {R} cm shorter. How long is the long ribbon in centimetres?
test: After reading {m}/{p} of a book, {a} still has {R} pages to read. How many pages are in the book?
test: {b} owns {R} more {t} than {a}, and {a} owns only {m}/{p} as many as {b}. Find how many {t} {b} owns.
test: A tank was full. Then {m}/{p} of the water was used, and {R} litres remain. How many litres does the full tank hold?
test: A baker sold {m}/{p} of the buns by noon. {R} buns were still on the shelf. How many buns had the baker baked?
exercise: {a} from Ohio spent {m}/{p} of {a.his} pocket money at the fair. {a.He} still has {R} dollars. How much money, in dollars, did {a.he} have to begin with?
exercise: How many children are in a class in Dublin if {m}/{p} of them are boys and {R} are girls?
exercise: {b} has {R} more {t} than {a}, and {a} has just {m}/{p} as many {t} as {b}. How many {t} has {b} got?
exercise: A farmer in Iowa sold {m}/{p} of his eggs at the market. {R} eggs remained. How many eggs did he have before the market?
exercise: {a} used {m}/{p} of a roll of tape and has {R} cm of tape remaining. How long was the roll, in centimetres?
exercise: A shop in Toronto sold {m}/{p} of its kites on Saturday, and {R} kites were not sold. How many kites did the shop have on Saturday morning?
exercise: {m}/{p} of the sheep on a farm in New Zealand are black, and the other {R} are white. How many sheep are on the farm altogether?
exercise: {a} gave away {m}/{p} of {a.his} {t} and kept the remaining {R}. How many {t} did {a.he} have in the beginning?
test: {a} in Sydney spends {m}/{p} of {a.his} savings on a skateboard, and {R} dollars are left over. What were {a.his} savings, in dollars?
test: Of the pupils on a school trip in Wales, {m}/{p} are boys and {R} are girls. How many pupils went on the trip?
test: {a}'s pile of {t} is only {m}/{p} the size of {b}'s pile, which has {R} {t} more. What is the number of {t} in {b}'s pile?
test: A water butt in a garden in Kent lost {m}/{p} of its water in a hot week, leaving {R} litres. How many litres were in it before?
test: {R} cupcakes were still left after a bake sale in Vermont at which {m}/{p} of the cupcakes were sold. How many cupcakes were there at the start of the sale?
test: A road crew in Alberta has paved {m}/{p} of a road, and {R} metres are still to be paved. How long is the whole road, in metres?
exercise: spent {m}/{p} of me money, had {R+u} left — no wait, {R} dollars left. how much i have to start with
exercise: {a} sold {m}/{p} of them {t}, got {R} left now. how many {t} {a.he} had before
exercise: {m}/{p} of our class is boys, {R} girls, oh and 2 teachers but they don't count. how many kids in the class
exercise: {b} got {R} more {t} than {a}, {a} only got {m}/{p} as many. how many {b} got then
test: {a} says the full tank is {R+m} litres cos {R} + {m}. nah that's wrong innit. {m}/{p} used up, {R} litres left, how much it hold full
test: mum spent {m}/{p} of her wages at the shops, {R} dollars left, bus was late again btw. how much she had
test: read like {m}/{p} of me book, still {R} pages to go. how many pages it got
exam: It is given that {a} expended {m}/{p} of {a.his} funds upon a book, a sum of {R} dollars remaining thereafter. Determine the amount of money in the possession of {a} at the outset, in dollars.
exam: Whereas {m}/{p} of the children enrolled in a class are boys, and the number of girls is {R}, ascertain the total number of children enrolled in the class.
exam: Ascertain the original number of {t} in a box from which {m}/{p} of the {t} were removed, {R} {t} remaining therein.
exam: A full tank of water is drawn upon until {m}/{p} of its contents have been consumed, whereupon {R} litres remain. State the original volume of water in the tank, in litres.
exercise: Grandad passed away and left {a} some money. {a} gave {m}/{p} of it to charity and kept {R} dollars. How many dollars did Grandad leave {a}?
exercise: Since Mum was made redundant, the family has spent {m}/{p} of its savings and has {R} dollars left. How many dollars were the savings at first?
test: {a} "borrowed" — five-finger discount more like — {m}/{p} of the {t} in the tin, and there's {R} {t} left. how many were in it, eh?
